# Code owners for fantasy-pressbox
#
# GitHub uses this file to decide who must review a pull request. The branch
# ruleset on `main` requires an approving review from a code owner, so every
# change merged into main needs sign-off from someone listed here.
#
# Syntax: <file pattern>  <owner>
# The LAST matching pattern wins, so put the most specific rules at the bottom.

# Ryan owns everything by default.
*                       @ryrykeith

# The rules below are redundant while one person owns the whole repository.
# They are here so that adding a second maintainer later is a one-line change
# rather than a rethink, and so it is obvious which areas matter most.

# Editorial behaviour: prompts and tunable configuration decide what the
# publication actually says.
/prompts/               @ryrykeith
/config/                @ryrykeith

# Anything touching secrets, ignore rules or repository policy.
/.github/               @ryrykeith
/.gitignore             @ryrykeith
/.env.example           @ryrykeith
